/**
\page org_mitk_views_exampleview Example View

The Example View demonstrates how a plugin contributes a view to the MITK
Workbench. It applies the example image filter to a selected image and lets you
paint on the result.

\tableofcontents

\section org_mitk_views_exampleview_usage Usage

-# Load an image into the application.
-# Select it in the image selector at the top of the view.
-# Choose an offset and press "Add Offset". A new image node named
   "&lt;image&gt; (Offset: &lt;offset&gt;)" is added to the Data Manager, holding the
   input image with the offset added to every voxel.
-# The new image has a painting interactor attached: hold the Ctrl key and click
   or drag in a 2-D window to set voxels under the cursor to the minimum value.

\section org_mitk_views_exampleview_developers Notes for developers

This page is the context-sensitive help that appears when the user presses F1 in
the view. Doxygen locates it by its page id, which must equal the view id
declared in \c plugin.xml with the dots replaced by underscores
(\c org.mitk.views.exampleview becomes \c org_mitk_views_exampleview). Use this
page as the model for documenting your own view.

*/
